+## Mid-morning: Qasr Ibrahim and the Al-Koot District
 
-Head east to [Jabal Al-Qarah](/en/attractions/jabal-al-qarah/), the geological wonder at the heart of the oasis. Midday is no obstacle here — its caves **stay cool in summer and warm in winter**, a refuge when the heat peaks. At the mountain's foot in Al-Qarah village sits [Dougha Al-Gharash](/en/attractions/duqat-algharash/), the pottery house handed down through the Al-Gharash family, one of the Kingdom's best-known homes of the craft.
+Return to central Hofuf for [Qasr Ibrahim](/en/attractions/qasr-ibrahim/) — the fortress that gathers mosque, garrison and tower beneath one wall; the mid-morning light brings out its architecture and inner courtyard. Close by lies the historic Al-Koot district, home to [Bayt Al-Bay'ah](/en/attractions/baiah/) — the Al-Mulla family house built by Al-Ahsa's judge, Sheikh Abdulrahman bin Omar Al-Mulla, in 1203 AH / 1789 CE, where the people of Al-Ahsa pledged allegiance to King Abdulaziz in 1913 and joined the Saudi state; today it is a museum.
 
